\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{From one-time measurements to histories}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{The retained coordinate in \ref{fdip-00HK} has an exact equilibrium
distribution, yet its past and future remain conditionally dependent after its present
value is given. The [full Euclidean correlations](fdip-00HB) keep the intermediate
configurations. Which observations survive when each spatial slice is projected, and
how do time reflection and translation act on those histories?}
